00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:54.863
It's awesome, it's my favorite one.

00:05:54.863 --> 00:05:55.696
It's so funny.

00:05:55.696 --> 00:05:58.440
- Brendan O'Carroll, Mrs.
Brown. He's huge in Europe.

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.273
- Oh my God. I know.

00:05:59.273 --> 00:06:00.880
I love it, it's amazing.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.590
It's so great. And wait,
this is awesome too.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.190
Shout out to Ma-delle 90.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.680
- [Tyler] Ma-delle, Ma-delle, yeah.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.680
- My favorite thing is you said 90.

00:06:11.903 --> 00:06:14.640
- She does. So Adele did 30.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.370
That's Madea's, 90 year old album.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.070
So, and her song was called "Hellerr".

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:21.507
- Hellerr. You should do a music...

00:06:22.545 --> 00:06:24.458
- Album? Do a whole album.

00:06:24.458 --> 00:06:26.620
- Yes, cover them all.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.453
- That's great.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.286
- [Kelly] And change it.

00:06:28.286 --> 00:06:30.240
Wait, speaking of how positive you are

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.700
and I love your messages. I love this.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.880
You once said negativity screams,

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:35.525
and positivity whispers.

00:06:35.525 --> 00:06:36.358
- Yeah.

00:06:36.358 --> 00:06:38.920
- That is such a powerful statement.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.710
And I want you to talk about it a bit,

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:43.110
but I also wanted to
say, it's hilarious to me

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.820
because there's this song
that recently came out.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:45.851
I might say her name wrong, I'm so sorry.

00:06:45.851 --> 00:06:46.730
Avery Anna, I think is her name

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:48.760
and it's a song called narcissist

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:51.530
and there was this line in
it that's kind of similar

00:06:51.530 --> 00:06:55.180
and it's, "you lose your
voice when you yell too much".

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.880
And I love that physically
you lose your voice

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.330
when you yell too much, but
all also you lose your power.

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.509
'Cause I feel like people
confuse power and force.

00:07:01.509 --> 00:07:02.380
- Yes.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.960
- And it's so powerful, the
whispering is more powerful.

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:09.787
- I've never seen really
powerful people yell. Right?

00:07:09.787 --> 00:07:10.620
- [Kelly] Exactly.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:11.950
- When you're powerful,
you make decisions.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.890
You don't do all the yelling
and screaming, right?

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:16.229
But no, I said that because everything

00:07:16.229 --> 00:07:18.730
that bombards us all
day long is negativity,

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:20.920
if you think about it, on
your phone, on the news,

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.580
everything is negativity,
and it gets so much attention

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.060
and so much pickup, right?

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.790
But if somebody does
something kind for someone

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.760
or helps them rebuild a
house that burned down

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:30.840
or saves someone's dog or,

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:33.240
you don't hear that everywhere. Right?

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.670
So I wish there was more balance of it

00:07:35.670 --> 00:07:37.550
because we're bombarded
with all the negativity.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.560
I wish there was more
balance of the positivity

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:40.950
so people could start to feel good.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:42.639
That's why I wanted to bring Madea back.

00:07:42.639 --> 00:07:46.120
- Me too and I feel like unfortunately

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.830
it's a bit of supply and
demand. We have to demand that.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.557
'Cause the reason why they
supply it is cause people...

00:07:51.557 --> 00:07:54.050
They like a train wreck,
it's like they like it,

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:56.990
